## 13. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The application is not complete merely because it builds or displays a dashboard.

It is complete when the following conditions are satisfied, to the extent supported by the configured environment:

**Generation:** The parent can generate separate weekly debate packs for both children.

**Educational quality:** Each pack has a suitable motion, balanced arguments, both complete sample speeches, rebuttals, examples, and practice exercises.

**Coaching:** The parent receives actionable guidance and confidence-building activities.

**Research integrity:** Sources are presented honestly, and unverified claims are not misrepresented as established facts.

**Persistence:** Accepted topics, generated packs, and assessment records survive the intended persistence boundary.

**History:** Previous topics can be retrieved, reviewed, and used to avoid repetition.

**Progress:** The parent can assess performance and set a realistic next goal.

**Printing:** The full preparation pack can be printed without losing essential content.

**Security:** API credentials remain private and unnecessary child data is not collected.

**Reliability:** Failures are handled gracefully, and previously saved work is protected from accidental loss.

**Usability:** A parent can move from opening the app to preparing a complete debate session without needing to modify the code.

